{
  "readme": "# 🫥 NoMount Suite\n\nLoads root modules without mounting anything, RRO overlays included. No\n`overlayfs`, no `tmpfs`: the **Prism** kernel engine redirects VFS lookups, so\nnothing shows up in `/proc/mounts`. It is a metamodule.\n\n> **Beta.** Reports from other phones, managers and odd modules move it to\n> stable. `nomount export` builds the bundle, hide list redacted.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/status.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/status.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Status\"></a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/hiding.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/hiding.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Hiding\"></a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/rules.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/rules.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Rules\"></a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/diagnostics.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/diagnostics.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Checks\"></a></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/duckdetector.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/duckdetector.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Duck Detector\"></a></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Status</b></sub></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Hiding</b></sub></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Rules</b></sub></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Checks</b></sub></td>\n    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Duck Detector</b></sub></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n## Install\n\nEach [release](https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/releases/latest) has two zips:\n\n| Zip | For |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `00_NoMount-Module` | A kernel with the engine built in: the [`BakaSu`](https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-BakaSu_NMS/releases), [`KsuNext`](https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-KsuNext_NMS/releases) or [`SukiSu`](https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-SukiSu_NMS/releases) OnePlus kernels, or your own build with `CONFIG_NOMOUNT=y` from [`hookless/`](hookless/) |\n| `01_NoMount-Module-LKM` | A stock GKI kernel. It loads the engine as a module at boot (android12-5.10 to android17-6.18) |\n\nFlash it from your manager, reboot, then check from a root shell:\n\n```sh\nalias nomount=/data/adb/modules/meta-nomount/bin/arm64-v8a/nomount\nnomount check      # want: verdict: clean, 0 failed, 0 unmeasured\n```\n\nNeeds arm64 and KernelSU (or a fork) or Magisk. SUSFS is not needed. Updates\nare the same flash and keep your settings.\n\n## Safe Guard boot\n\nLet it boot twice more: after three failed boots the Suite parks itself. To\npark it by hand from recovery:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p /data/adb/nomount && touch /data/adb/nomount/disabled\n```\n\n## Commands\n\nThe WebUI does all of this. From a shell: `nomount check`, `reload`,\n`uid block <pkg>`, `whiteout add <path>`, `export`. `nomount --help` has the\nrest. To report a problem, attach what **Checks → Developer tools → Export**\nwrites.\n\n## Building\n\n```sh\ncargo test && ANDROID_NDK_HOME=/path/to/ndk scripts/package.sh --build --version vX.Y.Z\n```\n\n## License and credits\n\nGPL-3.0, see [LICENSE](LICENSE). A rewrite of\n**[maxsteeel/nomount](https://github.com/maxsteeel/nomount)**. Thanks to\n[HymoFS](https://github.com/Anatdx/HymoFS), [A7mdwassa](https://github.com/A7mdwassa),\n[ZQZCC](https://github.com/ZQZCC), [backslashxx](https://github.com/backslashxx),\n[KernelSU](https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU), SukiSU-Ultra,\n[SUSFS](https://gitlab.com/simonpunk/susfs4ksu) and every tester.\n\nModifying a kernel can brick a phone or lose data. Use at your own risk.\n",
  "readmeHTML": "<h1>🫥 NoMount Suite</h1>\n\n<p>Loads root modules without mounting anything, RRO overlays included. No</p>\n<p><code>overlayfs</code>, no <code>tmpfs</code>: the <b>Prism</b> kernel engine redirects VFS lookups, so</p>\n<p>nothing shows up in <code>/proc/mounts</code>. It is a metamodule.</p>\n\n<p>> <b>Beta.</b> Reports from other phones, managers and odd modules move it to</p>\n<p>> stable. <code>nomount export</code> builds the bundle, hide list redacted.</p>\n\n<p><table></p>\n<p>  <tr></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/status.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/status.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Status\"></a></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/hiding.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/hiding.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Hiding\"></a></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/rules.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/rules.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Rules\"></a></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/diagnostics.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/diagnostics.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Checks\"></a></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/blob/main/docs/screenshots/duckdetector.jpg\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/main/docs/screenshots/duckdetector.jpg\" width=\"155\" alt=\"Duck Detector\"></a></td></p>\n<p>  </tr></p>\n<p>  <tr></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Status</b></sub></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Hiding</b></sub></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Rules</b></sub></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Checks</b></sub></td></p>\n<p>    <td align=\"center\"><sub><b>Duck Detector</b></sub></td></p>\n<p>  </tr></p>\n<p></table></p>\n\n<h2>Install</h2>\n\n<p>Each <a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/NoMount-Suite/releases/latest\">release</a> has two zips:</p>\n\n<p>| Zip | For |</p>\n<p>| :--- | :--- |</p>\n<p>| <code>00_NoMount-Module</code> | A kernel with the engine built in: the <a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-BakaSu_NMS/releases\"><code>BakaSu</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-KsuNext_NMS/releases\"><code>KsuNext</code></a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/Bouteillepleine/OnePlus-SukiSu_NMS/releases\"><code>SukiSu</code></a> OnePlus kernels, or your own build with <code>CONFIG_NOMOUNT=y</code> from <a href=\"hookless/\"><code>hookless/</code></a> |</p>\n<p>| <code>01_NoMount-Module-LKM</code> | A stock GKI kernel. It loads the engine as a module at boot (android12-5.10 to android17-6.18) |</p>\n\n<p>Flash it from your manager, reboot, then check from a root shell:</p>\n\n<pre>alias nomount=/data/adb/modules/meta-nomount/bin/arm64-v8a/nomount\nnomount check      # want: verdict: clean, 0 failed, 0 unmeasured</pre>\n\n<p>Needs arm64 and KernelSU (or a fork) or Magisk. SUSFS is not needed. Updates</p>\n<p>are the same flash and keep your settings.</p>\n\n<h2>Safe Guard boot</h2>\n\n<p>Let it boot twice more: after three failed boots the Suite parks itself. To</p>\n<p>park it by hand from recovery:</p>\n\n<pre>mkdir -p /data/adb/nomount &amp;&amp; touch /data/adb/nomount/disabled</pre>\n\n<h2>Commands</h2>\n\n<p>The WebUI does all of this. From a shell: <code>nomount check</code>, <code>reload</code>,</p>\n<p><code>uid block <pkg></code>, <code>whiteout add <path></code>, <code>export</code>. <code>nomount --help</code> has the</p>\n<p>rest. To report a problem, attach what <b>Checks → Developer tools → Export</b></p>\n<p>writes.</p>\n\n<h2>Building</h2>\n\n<pre>cargo test &amp;&amp; ANDROID_NDK_HOME=/path/to/ndk scripts/package.sh --build --version vX.Y.Z</pre>\n\n<h2>License and credits</h2>\n\n<p>GPL-3.0, see <a href=\"LICENSE\">LICENSE</a>. A rewrite of</p>\n<p><b><a href=\"https://github.com/maxsteeel/nomount\">maxsteeel/nomount</a></b>. Thanks to</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/Anatdx/HymoFS\">HymoFS</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/A7mdwassa\">A7mdwassa</a>,</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/ZQZCC\">ZQZCC</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/backslashxx\">backslashxx</a>,</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU\">KernelSU</a>, SukiSU-Ultra,</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://gitlab.com/simonpunk/susfs4ksu\">SUSFS</a> and every tester.</p>\n\n<p>Modifying a kernel can brick a phone or lose data. Use at your own risk.</p>",
